==========================================================================
AUTONOMY DISCLOSURE
==========================================================================

Parts of this product are designed to operate on software repositories
and continuous-integration systems on the user's behalf (repository
hygiene passes, CI triage, budget-capped auto-retry and auto-repair
rounds, round ledger with rollback and salvage). Deployment is the
operator's decision; the operator is responsible for the credentials,
scopes, and repository authorization they grant to the tool. Budget
caps, the fail-loud rule, and the append-only experience ledger exist
so that every autonomous action can be bounded and audited. See
docs/license-protocol-v1.0-20261114.md.

